  {
   "id": 522430,
   "is_answer_order_important": true,
   "stimulus_html": "",
   "stem_html": "In the collection of a botanical garden, plants are classified according to the environments in which they thrive. Compare descriptions of plants and environments below. What plant in which environment would have large leaves that are covered with a thick upper cuticle, exhibit wide flat blades, and possess large air spaces (chambers) within mesophyll tissue?",
   "answers": [
    {
     "id": 1022599,
     "content_html": "a water lily floating on water"
    },
    {
     "id": 1022600,
     "content_html": "a pine tree growing in the cold and dry taiga"
    },
    {
     "id": 1022601,
     "content_html": "a cactus growing in a hot, sunny, and dry environment"
    },
    {
     "id": 1022602,
     "content_html": "an orchid hanging from a tree in a tropical forest"
    }
   ],
